# counter harness. One force call is one HarnessCounter entry.
# The initial Hessian is a central difference of the harness gradient on the free atoms.
# Each displaced gradient is a force call. Later steps use the Bofill update and cost one gradient.
# The Hessian index is analytic and is not a search call.
# The legacy mean is the half-even mean of starts at the force stop and under the cap.
# v2 success also requires Hessian index 1.
# A curvature is negative only below -max(force_norm, 1e-8*||H||_F, 1e-6).
# LJ38 removes rigid modes. The Pt island keeps fixed atoms out of the matrix and does not project rigid modes.
# OptKing's own convergence test is not the stop. The stop is the problem Euclidean force norm.
# Each worker uses one BLAS thread.
# OptKing transition-state step P_RFO in Cartesian coordinates on the free Pt atoms. The potential is the smooth-linear Morse of the problem file, with the frozen substrate held in place. full_hess_every is 0, so the first Hessian is computed and later steps use the Bofill update. The field default of full_hess_every is -1, a model Hessian and no harness Hessian. This revision has no step type named RS_PRFO. The initial Hessian is a central difference of the harness gradient on the free atoms, step 1e-5, and those evaluations are force calls. The stop is the problem Euclidean force norm 0.001. The force-call cap is 10000.
